# Paths this repo deliberately does NOT carry, each with the reason (WI-308).
#
# One line per entry: `<path> — <reason>`. Blank lines and `#` comments ignored.
#
# Two readers share it, which is the point — the fact is stated once:
#   - `tests/test_dogfood_sync.py` — the scaffold-omission declaration: a
#     `bootstrap.py` MAPPING destination that is absent here must be listed, and
#     an entry whose path MATERIALIZES must be removed (a test enforces both).
#   - `check_doc_refs.py` — prose naming one of these is UNTRACED, not dangling.
#     Before WI-308 those references were 12 of this repo's 22 dangling findings,
#     each of them a fact already stated here.
#
# This is a DECLARATION, not a suppression list: every line carries its reason,
# a materialized path fails the honesty test, and nothing here is exempt from
# the checker — it is reclassified, counted, and printable with
# `--show-untraced`. A path that is simply ROT does not belong here; it belongs
# fixed (`docs/next-wi`, retired by WI-180, is the worked example).
#
# A reason beginning `LIFECYCLE:` declares a path whose PRESENCE is a legal,
# documented state (a claim dir while work is claimed, a pause marker while
# paused): the honesty test exempts it from the materialize-guard — asserting
# absence deadlocked the §2.3 parallel-claims queue, since every composed tree
# holds the OTHER branches' claim dirs (WI-369) — while `check_doc_refs.py`
# still classifies prose naming it when absent. Everything unmarked keeps the
# exact guard, including every retired surface.

docs/requirements/work-items.csv — retired at the Phase 2c authority flip (concurrency-restructure §2/§7): the work-item registry is the docs/work/ spec folder; prose naming the CSV before 2026-07-29 is history, and a migrating adopter converts theirs with scripts/wi_convert.py.
docs/work/archive/ — retired at WI-384's state-model flip (concurrency-v2 §B2): the folder held BOTH terminal states and so needed a `disposition` attribute to tell them apart, and splitting it into docs/work/complete/ and docs/work/cancelled/ is what deleted that attribute, its validator and both raise paths. Prose naming archive/ before 2026-08-01 is history. Deliberately NOT marked LIFECYCLE: this path must never materialize again, so the honesty guard here is the same reconciliation signal the loaders enforce — a spec closed into archive/ by a branch cut before the flip is a named, loud error, not a silent skip.
docs/archive/specs/complete/ — a destination concurrency-v2 §B2 NAMES but this repo deliberately does not carry: §B2 asked the spec-of-record home to mirror the terminal folders WI-384 gave the registry. WI-391 measured that mirror and REFUTED it (2026-08-01, review-confirmed): the spec→folder mapping is not total (92 of 111 archived specs resolve to complete, 3 to cancelled, 16 to nothing), it is contradictory for at least one file (research-knowledge.2026-07-29.md has citers in both terminal states), it has no regenerator to gate freshness against, and for every attributable spec docs/work/ already answers shipped-or-cancelled by location. So this path is absent BY DECISION, not by omission. Whether §B2's sentence is struck or restated is OI-11 (pending); WI-391 is parked queued+blockref on it. Do NOT delete this line to tidy up — the WI-391 spec's own title names this path, so removing the declaration turns it into a dangling reference (measured: +2 under check_doc_refs --strict). Deliberately unmarked, so the exact materialize-guard still applies: if the mirror is ever built, removing this line is the deliberate act that records it.
docs/archive/specs/cancelled/ — the second half of the same §B2 destination pair; see the line above for the measurement, the OI-11 referent and the reason neither line may be deleted while WI-391's spec text names them.

